@startuml runtime_result_waiting
title Bound and Read Results for Fixed Runtime Targets
' Contract: pi-mono-java-design 2ee2a3211da68ad87b0d9cab353e691b00bdaebd
' Java baseline: 43a8e000; implementation: 606e27a1, f5e904aa and bb8047fe
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeResultWaitRegistry.java#reserve #bind #claimTargets #deliver
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeResultPollingService.java#poll #notifyCommitted
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/dto/ResultWaitTargetDTO.java#claimId
' Pi baseline: 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3
' Pi source: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts#runAgentLoop
' Observed behavior: queries run outside the registry lock and can finish after a group is replaced.
' Design reason: a generation claim prevents an old read from closing a new response for the same target.
' Java divergence: shared database result waiting is a CampusClaw architecture change.
actor "Request handler" as Handler
participant "Bounded response registry" as Registry
participant "Periodic or local notifier" as Poller
database "Committed result repository" as Database
participant "Request response" as Response
Handler -> Registry: Reserve one response slot
note over Handler: HTTP acceptance wiring is a later integration.
Handler -> Registry: Bind accepted exact target, mode and cursor
Poller -> Poller: Check shared database failure backoff
Poller -> Registry: Claim bounded fair groups with unique claimId
Registry --> Poller: Exact target, mode, minimum cursor, claimId
Poller -> Database: Read committed segment or actual execution terminal
Database --> Poller: Ordered complete events and terminal state
Poller -> Registry: Deliver only to the same active claim generation
Registry -> Response: Per-response events after its own cursor
Response -> Registry: Release on close or wait expiry
note over Registry, Response
  Callbacks run outside the registry lock.
  Response expiry does not terminate the Agent.
  Late results cannot affect a replacement group.
end note
@enduml
